From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:51:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 176/184] Bound the EMUDESK.INF window-path copy

The #W handler copies a path out of the file into a fixed 114-byte
field with nothing but a '@' to stop it. A file that ends mid-line, or
one line longer than the field, runs off the end of pth_save and through
the saved window state behind it.

Survivable when EMUDESK.INF lived on a disk the desktop wrote itself.
Not survivable now that this machine reads it first from an eight
kilobyte internal backup RAM, where a half-finished write truncates it.
---
 desk/deskapp.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/desk/deskapp.c b/desk/deskapp.c
index 2f57a3f..7728f9f 100644
--- a/desk/deskapp.c
+++ b/desk/deskapp.c
@@ -917,9 +917,23 @@ void app_start(void)
 /* */
                 pcurr += 4;             /* skip no-longer-used field */
                 ptmp = pws->pth_save;
-                while(*pcurr != '@')
+                /* Bounded, and it was not.
+                 *
+                 * This copies a path out of a file into a fixed 114-byte
+                 * field with nothing but a '@' to stop it. A file that
+                 * ends mid-line -- or one line longer than the field --
+                 * runs off the end of pth_save, through the rest of the
+                 * saved window state behind it, and on through whatever
+                 * follows. That was survivable when EMUDESK.INF lived on
+                 * a disk written by the desktop itself; it is a real
+                 * hazard once the file can come off an eight-kilobyte
+                 * backup RAM that a half-finished write can truncate. */
+                while (*pcurr && *pcurr != '@'
+                       && ptmp < pws->pth_save + LEN_ZPATH - 1)
                     *ptmp++ = *pcurr++;
                 *ptmp = '\0';
+                while (*pcurr && *pcurr != '@')     /* the rest, if any */
+                    pcurr++;
                 wincnt += 1;
             }
             break;
